.TH "OSTRYA" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya \- \%Command\-line \%front\-end for the ostrya library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\%Command\-line \%front\-end for the ostrya library.
.PP
ostrya reads and writes ostree repositories. A repository keeps file trees as commits. Each file, directory, and commit is stored as objects, and the \%SHA\-256 checksum of an object is its name. A ref is a name that points to a commit. The \%on\-disk format is the format of the \fB\%ostree\fR command.
.PP
Each subcommand operates on one repository. The command finds the repository in this order: the \%\-\-repo option, the current directory, and the \fB\%OSTREE_REPO\fR environment variable. Run \fB\%ostrya <COMMAND> \-\-help\fR to see the options of a subcommand.
.SH OPTIONS
The options below are global. Each one is accepted before and after
the subcommand name.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fIREPO\fR
The path of the repository to operate on.
.IP
The option is accepted before and after the subcommand name. If both positions give a value, the value after the name wins. Without this option, the command opens the current directory if it is a repository. Else it opens the path in \fB\%OSTREE_REPO\fR if that path is a repository. If no source gives a repository, the command prints its usage text and \fB\%error: Command requires a \-\-repo argument\fR, then exits \%1.
.IP
\fB\%init\fR creates a new repository only at an explicit \%\-\-repo. Without the option, \fB\%init\fR reuses a repository that it finds in the current directory or at \fB\%OSTREE_REPO\fR\&. Each other subcommand exits \%1 if an explicit \%\-\-repo does not open as a repository.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Write extra information to standard error.
.IP
Most subcommands write the line \fB\%ostrya: using repository PATH\fR when they open the repository. \fB\%push\fR and \fB\%push\-tree\fR also write a statistics line after the push. \fB\%receive\fR and \fB\%send\fR write nothing more.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version information and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBostrya\-init\fR(1)
Initialize a new empty repository
.TP
\fBostrya\-commit\fR(1)
Commit a tree into the repository and print the new commit checksum
.TP
\fBostrya\-checkout\fR(1)
Check a commit out onto the file system, or write its composefs image
.TP
\fBostrya\-export\fR(1)
Write the tree of a commit as a tar stream, to stdout or to \%\-\-output
.TP
\fBostrya\-refs\fR(1)
List, create, or delete refs
.TP
\fBostrya\-rev\-parse\fR(1)
Print the commit checksum that a revision names
.TP
\fBostrya\-cat\fR(1)
Write the content of files of a commit to stdout
.TP
\fBostrya\-show\fR(1)
Print the report of an object, or one part of its commit metadata
.TP
\fBostrya\-log\fR(1)
Show the log that starts at a commit or ref
.TP
\fBostrya\-ls\fR(1)
List the file paths of a commit
.TP
\fBostrya\-config\fR(1)
Read or write a repository configuration value
.TP
\fBostrya\-remote\fR(1)
Manage the configured remotes and their trusted GPG keys
.TP
\fBostrya\-prune\fR(1)
Delete the objects that no ref or commit of the repository reaches
.TP
\fBostrya\-fsck\fR(1)
Verify object integrity and completeness across every commit
.TP
\fBostrya\-diff\fR(1)
Report the paths that changed between two revisions or directories
.TP
\fBostrya\-sign\fR(1)
Add, verify, or delete signatures on a commit
.TP
\fBostrya\-summary\fR(1)
Regenerate, sign, or verify the repository summary
.TP
\fBostrya\-static\-delta\fR(1)
List, generate, apply, or index static deltas
.TP
\fBostrya\-pull\fR(1)
Fetch refs and their objects from a remote over HTTP or ssh
.TP
\fBostrya\-pull\-local\fR(1)
Import refs and their objects from another local repository
.TP
\fBostrya\-receive\fR(1)
Receive one push session over standard input and standard output
.TP
\fBostrya\-push\fR(1)
Push commits to a remote over ssh or HTTP and update its refs
.TP
\fBostrya\-push\-tree\fR(1)
Push a directory as one commit over ssh or HTTP and set the remote refs
.TP
\fBostrya\-serve\fR(1)
Serve the repository over HTTP as an archive repository for pull
.TP
\fBostrya\-send\fR(1)
Serve one pull session over standard input and standard output
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBOSTREE_REPO\fR
The repository to operate on when \fB\-\-repo\fR is not given and the
current directory is not a repository.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create an archive repository, commit a directory to the ref \fBmain\fR, and
show the log of the ref:
.PP
.nf
ostrya \-\-repo=repo init \-\-mode=archive
ostrya \-\-repo=repo commit \-b main \-s 'First commit' tree/
ostrya \-\-repo=repo log main
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\-config\fR(1),
\fBostrya\-repo\fR(5)
